course: dictionary
lesson: 1536
title: Certify: officially saying it is true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To certify something is to say officially that it is true or correct. Someone in charge checks first, then confirms it. «The doctor certified that he was ill.» The doctor checked him, so it is now an official fact that he is ill.
explain: Certify can also mean giving someone an official paper that proves what they have learned. «She was certified as a lifeguard.» Her certificate is the paper, and it shows she passed the test. Certify is the verb, certificate is the noun, and certified is the word that describes the person or thing.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. Words like officially, paper and proof are clues. In a news report, the sentence «Congress certified it, which means officially confirmed it» explains itself. Check your meaning by swapping it in: officially confirmed it still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Certify means to officially say that something is true or correct.
fact: «Certified» can mean a person has an official paper proving their training, such as a lifeguard's certificate.
fact: «Certified organic» means an official check has shown that food meets a set standard.
fact: A certificate is the official paper itself. Certification is the process of certifying something.
fact: In a news report, «Congress certified it» means the lawmakers officially confirmed it.
exercise: «The doctor certified that he was ill.» What does certified mean here? | *Officially said it was true | Ran away from him | Gave him a present | Made a loud noise
exercise: «She was certified as a lifeguard.» What does this tell us about her? | She is a slow swimmer | She owns a big boat | She has lost her badge | *She trained and passed a test
exercise: Jayden sees «certified organic» on a bag of carrots. What does it tell him? | The carrots are very old | The carrots are very small | The carrots are a secret | *An official check showed the carrots meet a standard
test: In «Congress certified it, which means officially confirmed it», what does certified mean? | *Officially confirmed it | Forgot it | Lost it | Ignored it
test: Which word is the noun for the official paper? | certify | certified | *certificate | certifying
exam: Which sentence uses certify with the right meaning? | «He certified the rain by running.» | «The dog certified its bed.» | *«The teacher certified that the test results were correct.» | «She certified the cake with a big smile.»
